## Completed Stage-F result

Primary two_concepts architecture omnibus:

- centered-logit fidelity: F(15,1485)=77.0874, partial eta^2=0.4378, Holm p=2.40e-173;
- probability error reduction: F(15,1485)=656.7002, partial eta^2=0.8690, p numerically underflowed to 0.

Fresh bridge tiny_gmp - plain2_w16_gmp:

- centered-logit B difference +0.162258, 95% CI [+0.149701,+0.174815];
- probability-error B difference +0.889596, 95% CI [+0.862118,+0.917073].

Interpretation: architecture dependence is decisively reproduced. Pooling is a major modifier but its direction flips by backbone; under GMP the first downstream convolution explains most of the Tiny-vs-plain difference, while additional plain depth from 2 to 4 adds little. Residual connectivity is not a major driver. BatchNorm and width are context/metric dependent. See `RESEARCH_STATUS.md` for the full interpretation.

## Manuscript

`paper/main.tex` is intentionally a pre-Stage-F snapshot.

Do not perform the outcome-dependent rewrite until Stage F is complete. Follow `paper/REVISION_PLAN.md`.

Key planned changes:

- integrate metric-sensitivity audit prominently;
- explicitly discuss treatment-dependent normalization scale;
